      "head_commit": {
        "id": "fb595cdcd71ba4e97134f6eb103dd4dcc6a5e57a",
        "tree_id": "c32f121590ba4d3425f730e1a6afcc288d702b2e",
        "message": "feat(SEC-001): ingress gate, rate limits and GM audit\n\nUntrusted bytes go through decodeFrame, then a fixed refusal chain: kind,\nversion, rate, sequence. Every rejection carries a counted reason code —\nmalformed, unknown-kind, wrong-version, client-snapshot, rate-limited or\nnon-monotonic-seq. A client-sent snapshot is always refused (I1).\n\nFixed-window rate limit admits 30 intents per 30-tick window: a 200-message\nburst gives 30 admitted and 170 RATE_LIMIT, never a delayed flood. forget()\non logout clears sequence and rate state.\n\nA GM action needs a non-empty reason; an accepted one writes a frozen entry\nwith actor id, tick, reason and an FNV-1a hash. No reason writes nothing.\n\nThe threat model names seven residual risks verbatim: no auth, no TLS, the\ngate is NOT wired into attachRooms (SEC-002), in-memory counters only, no\nsocket flood test, retention is OPS-001, no statistical anti-cheat.\nGDD-SECURITY therefore does not claim 0 unvalidated message paths.\n\nGDD-SECURITY 0.3 (I9), corrupted §18 table repaired. The blueprint acc\npnpm test --filter @strata/security could never run; repaired to a real\nvitest command with its own config under tests/security/ (eleventh form).\n\nAcceptance: security 10/10, main 142/142, verify 17/17, tracer green.\n\nAgent: security-auditor\nTask: SEC-001",
        "timestamp": "2026-11-18T09:50:41Z",
